# Keep line endings out of the search index.
#
# Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout for anything it thinks is text.
# For this index that is not a cosmetic difference, it is a silent failure:
#
#   bm25-vocab.txt is one term per line and is split on "\n" when loaded. After
#   CRLF conversion every term gains a trailing "\r", so no query term ever
#   matches one. The keyword arm returns zero results, throws nothing, and logs
#   nothing -- answers just get quietly worse for everyone who cloned, while
#   working perfectly on the machine that built the index.
#
#   The .i32/.u8/.i8 files are raw typed arrays. A single byte inserted anywhere
#   shifts every value after it, so a misdetection there corrupts the embeddings
#   outright rather than degrading them.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion. binary also disables diffing, which
# is what you want for a 40 MB blob of float data.

data/index/**            -text
data/index/*.i32         binary
data/index/*.i8          binary
data/index/*.u8          binary
data/index/*.jsonl       -text
data/index/bm25-vocab.txt -text

# The OCR sidecars use \f as a page separator and are read back byte for byte.
data/ocr-cache/*.txt     -text

# Normal source files: let Git normalise these as usual.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
